Package: zanicc
Title: Bayesian nonparametric regression models for zero-inflated
    count-compositional data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("André F. B.", "Menezes", , "andrefelipemaringa@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3320-9834")),
    person("Keefe", "Murphy", role = "ctb",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5668-7046"))
  )
Maintainer: André F. B. Menezes <andrefelipemaringa@gmail.com>
Description: Provides flexible Bayesian nonparametric regression models
    for zero-inflated count-compositional data, including the
    zero-and-N-inflated multinomial (ZANIM)-BART and ZANIM logistic-normal
    (ZANIM-LN)-BART models introduced by Menezes et al. (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2601.08067>. These models use ensembles of
    regression trees with Bayesian additive regression trees (BART) priors
    to capture complex relationships between covariates and the
    multivariate compositional counts. Bayesian inference for
    model-specific parameters is performed using efficient Markov chain
    Monte Carlo (MCMC) algorithms implemented in C++. The package also
    includes implementations for other related count-compositional models,
    particularly the multinomial logistic BART model of Murray (2021)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.2020.1813587> and the zero-and-N-inflated
    Dirichlet-multinomial linear regression model of Koslovsky (2023)
    <doi:10.1111/biom.13853>. Methods for conducting Bayesian
    posterior predictive checks and computing posterior predictions for
    new data are also provided. In addition, it provides efficient C++ 
    implementations for the finite-mixture probability mass functions of 
    the ZANIM and ZANIDM distributions as proposed by Menezes et al.
    (2025)<doi:10.1016/j.jmva.2025.105492>. Finally, the package also
    implements the Bayesian modular framework for pollen-based
    palaeoclimate reconstruction based on the ZANIM-LN-BART model
    developed by Menezes et al. (2026b)<doi:10.48550/arXiv.2609.08866>.
